<!-- -->: <!-- -->Revelation, Problem &amp; Therefore</option><option value="12">Block <!-- -->12<!-- -->: <!-- -->Midpoint Choice &amp; Action</option><option value="13">Block <!-- -->13<!-- -->: <!-- -->Consequences &amp; Complications</option><option value="14">Block <!-- -->14<!-- -->: <!-- -->Therefore, Choice &amp; Adjusted Plan</option><option value="15">Block <!-- -->15<!-- -->: <!-- -->Major Crisis &amp; All Is Lost</option><option value="16">Block <!-- -->16<!-- -->: <!-- -->Dark Night &amp; Revelation</option><option value="17">Block <!-- -->17<!-- -->: <!-- -->New Choice, Plan &amp; Preparation</option><option value="18">Block <!-- -->18<!-- -->: <!-- -->Action, Climax &amp; Immediate Result</option><option value="19">Block <!-- -->19<!-- -->: <!-- -->Fallout &amp; New Normal</option><option value="20">Block <!-- -->20<!-- -->: <!-- -->Remaining Questions &amp; Actions</option><option value="21">Block <!-- -->21<!-- -->: <!-- -->Final Choice &amp; Last Attempt</option><option value="22">Block <!-- -->22<!-- -->: <!-- -->Final Action &amp; Ultimate Stakes</option><option value="23">Block <!-- -->23<!-- -->: <!-- -->Resolution &amp; New Equilibrium</option><option value="24">Block <!-- -->24<!-- -->: <!-- -->Reflection &amp; Closing Image</option></select></label><label><span>Character entrance</span><select disabled=""></select></label></section><section class="_contextGrid_xqi1p_45"><article><strong>Story cause</strong><span>Why the block moves</span><p>Add the goal, conflict, action, and consequence in Story Planner.</p></article><article><strong>Emotional turn</strong><span>Meaning that needs screen evidence</span><p>Name the emotional change, then express it through behaviour, space, objects, dialogue, or reaction.</p></article><article><strong>Audience attention</strong><span>What the reader should track</span><p>Clarify what the audience expects and what changes that expectation.</p></article></section><section class="_scorePanel_xqi1p_46" aria-label="PageFlow draft signals"><div class="_scoreRing_xqi1p_186" style="--score:360deg"><strong>100</strong><span>draft signal</span></div><div class="_metricGrid_xqi1p_215"><div><strong>0</strong><span>action words</span></div><div><strong>0</strong><span>visual beats</span></div><div><strong>0</strong><span>words per sentence</span></div><div><strong>0</strong><span>dense paragraphs</span></div></div><p>This is an editorial signal, not a grade. Dialogue and character cues are excluded where screenplay formatting makes them identifiable.</p></section><div class="_workspace_xqi1p_244"><section class="_draftPanel_xqi1p_251"><div class="_sectionHeading_xqi1p_32"><p class="_kicker_xqi1p_54">Block <!-- -->1<!-- --> · <!-- -->Hook, Introduction &amp; Catalyst</p><h2>Write the movie the reader can see.</h2><p>Use exact nouns, active verbs, clear order, playable behaviour, and paragraph breaks that match visual turns.</p></div><label class="_field_xqi1p_277"><span>Page Draft</span><textarea rows="22"></textarea><small>Screenplay action, scene text, or a polished description pass. This edits the block&#x27;s shared Story text field.</small></label><div class="_twoColumns_xqi1p_313"><label class="_field_xqi1p_277"><span>Visible sequence</span><textarea rows="9"></textarea><small>Describe the image progression the Visual Board should preserve.</small></label><label class="_field_xqi1p_277"><span>PageFlow revision notes</span><textarea rows="9"></textarea><small>Record invisible information to externalize, beats to split, actions to sharpen, or justified exceptions.</small></label></div><div class="_entrancePanel_xqi1p_47"><div><p class="_kicker_xqi1p_54">Character entrance in motion</p><h3>No character selected</h3><p>Give the reader a concise first impression through condition, action, contradiction, clothing, or relationship to the space.</p></div><p class="_empty_xqi1p_409">Add characters in Story Planner to develop an entrance.</p></div></section><aside class="_diagnosticPanel_xqi1p_252"><div class="_sectionHeading_xqi1p_32"><p class="_kicker_xqi1p_54">Revision signals</p><h2>Inspect, do not obey blindly.</h2><p>Each signal asks whether the action line has become visible, direct, playable, and readable.</p></div><article class="_signalCard_xqi1p_48"><strong>Invisible or explanatory</strong><p>No common invisible-state terms detected in action text.</p></article><article class="_signalCard_xqi1p_48"><strong>Possible directing language</strong><p>No common camera or editing terms detected in action text.</p></article><article class="_signalCard_xqi1p_48"><strong>Weak action phrases</strong><p>No common delayed-action phrases detected in action text.</p></article><article class="_signalCard_xqi1p_48"><strong>Emotion labels to physicalize</strong><p>No common emotion labels detected in action text.</p></article><div class="_checklist_xqi1p_337"><h3>Five-pass rewrite</h3><ol><li><strong>Screen pass</strong><span>Can the audience see or hear every essential idea?</span></li><li><strong>Verb pass</strong><span>Can one exact action replace a weak phrase or explanation?</span></li><li><strong>Actor pass</strong><span>Does the character have behaviour to play rather than an emotion to imitate?</span></li><li><strong>Rhythm pass</strong><span>Does each paragraph contain one primary visual beat?</span></li><li><strong>Restraint pass</strong><span>Are you guiding attention without directing every shot?</span></li></ol></div><div class="_wordBank_xqi1p_49"><h3>Action families</h3><p>Use these as prompts for specificity, not as mandatory vocabulary.</p><div><span>advance</span><span>withdraw</span><span>block</span><span>grip</span><span>scan</span><span>flinch</span><span>crumple</span><span>snap</span><span>hover</span><span>brace</span><span>corner</span><span>release</span></div></div></aside></div><p class="_status_xqi1p_402" aria-live="polite">Loading the active PlotPickle project…</p></div></main><script id="_R_">import("/assets/index-DBCHrurJ.js")</script></body></html><script>self.__VINEXT_RSC_CHUNKS__=self.__VINEXT_RSC_CHUNKS__||[];self.__VINEXT_RSC_CHUNKS__.push("2:I[\"8c0f216c4604\",[],\"Children\",1]\n3:I[\"f08ec09499bf\",[],\"default\",1]\n4:I[\"96df7669e034\",[],\"default\",1]\n5:I[\"15c18cfaeeff\",[],\"LayoutSegmentProvider\",1]\n6:I[\"8c0f216c4604\",[],\"Slot\",1]\n7:I[\"593f344dc510\",[],\"RedirectBoundary\",1]\n:HL[\"/assets/index-DedKIDsC.css\",\"style\"]\n")</script><script>self.__VINEXT_RSC_CHUNKS__=self.__VINEXT_RSC_CHUNKS__||[];self.__VINEXT_RSC_CHUNKS__.push("0:{\"__route\":\"route:/pageflow\",\"__interceptionContext\":null,\"__layoutIds\":[\"layout:/\"],\"__rootLayout\":\"/\",\"page:/pageflow\":\"$L1\",\"layout:/\":[[[[\"$\",\"link\",\"css:/assets/index-DedKIDsC.css\",{\"rel\":\"stylesheet\",\"precedence\":\"vite-rsc/importer-resources\",\"href\":\"/assets/index-DedKIDsC.css\",\"data-rsc-css-href\":\"/assets/index-DedKIDsC.css\"}],\"$undefined\"],[\"$\",\"html\",null,{\"lang\":\"en\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"body\",null,{\"className\":\"__variable_geist_0gdoon9 __variable_geist_mono_08lusff antialiased\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{}],[\"$\",\"$L4\",null,{}]]}]}]],null],\"route:/pageflow\":[[[\"$\",\"meta\",null,{\"charSet\":\"utf-8\"}],[[\"$\",\"title\",\"0\",{\"children\":\"PlotPickle\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"description\",\"content\":\"Download PlotPickle Playhouse: a local-first story planner connecting Project Overview, Story Planner, Structure Map, Visual Board, and guided specialist engines through Bryan Harris's 24 Blocks method.\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"2\",{\"rel\":\"shortcut icon\",\"href\":\"/brand/favicon/favicon.ico\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"3\",{\"rel\":\"icon\",\"href\":\"/brand/favicon/plotpickle-icon-32.png\",\"sizes\":\"32x32\",\"type\":\"image/png\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"4\",{\"rel\":\"icon\",\"href\":\"/brand/favicon/plotpickle-icon-192.png\",\"sizes\":\"192x192\",\"type\":\"image/png\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"5\",{\"rel\":\"icon\",\"href