    </head><body class="__variable_geist_0gdoon9 __variable_geist_mono_08lusff antialiased"><main class="_page_lrrt8_1"><div class="_shell_lrrt8_10"><header class="_header_lrrt8_15"><div><p class="_kicker_lrrt8_62">PlotPickle Playhouse · Story alignment workspace</p><h1>Resonance Engine</h1><p>Turn the story&#x27;s central question into a pattern of character choices, block turns, images, locations, objects, and dialogue. Build cohesion without reducing the screenplay to a slogan.</p></div><div class="_actions_lrrt8_71"><a href="/" class="_secondaryButton_lrrt8_79">Back to PlotPickle</a><a href="/pageflow" class="_secondaryButton_lrrt8_79">Open PageFlow</a><a href="/voiceprint" class="_secondaryButton_lrrt8_79">Open Voiceprint</a><button class="_button_lrrt8_78" type="button">Export project</button></div></header><section class="_projectBar_lrrt8_16"><div class="_projectTitle_lrrt8_111"><strong>Untitled Story</strong><span>Project schema <!-- -->1.7.0<!-- --> · <!-- -->Planning</span></div><label><span>Resonance block</span><select><option value="1" selected="">Block <!-- -->1<!-- -->: <!-- -->Hook, Introduction &amp; Catalyst</option><option value="2">Block <!-- -->2<!-- -->: <!-- -->Problem, Stakes &amp; Philosophy</option><option value="3">Block <!-- -->3<!-- -->: <!-- -->Anti-theme, Want &amp; Choice</option><option value="4">Block <!-- -->4<!-- -->: <!-- -->Initial Plan, Action &amp; New Problem</option><option value="5">Block <!-- -->5<!-- -->: <!-- -->Adaptation, Revised Plan &amp; Raised Stakes</option><option value="6">Block <!-- -->6<!-- -->: <!-- -->Choice, Action &amp; Antagonist Hint</option><option value="7">Block <!-- -->7<!-- -->: <!-- -->New World &amp; Exploration</option><option value="8">Block <!-- -->8<!-- -->: <!-- -->Action, Rising Tension &amp; Problems</option><option value="9">Block <!-- -->9<!-- -->: <!-- -->Therefore, Choice &amp; Adjusted Plan</option><option value="10">Block <!-- -->10<!-- -->: <!-- -->Raised Stakes, Deeper Question &amp; Action</option><option value="11">Block <!-- -->11<!-- -->: <!-- -->Revelation, Problem &amp; Therefore</option><option value="12">Block <!-- -->12<!-- -->: <!-- -->Midpoint Choice &amp; Action</option><option value="13">Block <!-- -->13<!-- -->: <!-- -->Consequences &amp; Complications</option><option value="14">Block <!-- -->14<!-- -->: <!-- -->Therefore, Choice &amp; Adjusted Plan</option><option value="15">Block <!-- -->15<!-- -->: <!-- -->Major Crisis &amp; All Is Lost</option><option value="16">Block <!-- -->16<!-- -->: <!-- -->Dark Night &amp; Revelation</option><option value="17">Block <!-- -->17<!-- -->: <!-- -->New Choice, Plan &amp; Preparation</option><option value="18">Block <!-- -->18<!-- -->: <!-- -->Action, Climax &amp; Immediate Result</option><option value="19">Block <!-- -->19<!-- -->: <!-- -->Fallout &amp; New Normal</option><option value="20">Block <!-- -->20<!-- -->: <!-- -->Remaining Questions &amp; Actions</option><option value="21">Block <!-- -->21<!-- -->: <!-- -->Final Choice &amp; Last Attempt</option><option value="22">Block <!-- -->22<!-- -->: <!-- -->Final Action &amp; Ultimate Stakes</option><option value="23">Block <!-- -->23<!-- -->: <!-- -->Resolution &amp; New Equilibrium</option><option value="24">Block <!-- -->24<!-- -->: <!-- -->Reflection &amp; Closing Image</option></select></label><label><span>Character argument</span><select disabled=""></select></label></section><section class="_signalPanel_lrrt8_17" aria-label="Resonance alignment signal"><div class="_signalCopy_lrrt8_50"><p class="_kicker_lrrt8_62">Alignment signal</p><div class="_signalNumber_lrrt8_160">0<span>/100</span></div><p>This is a coverage prompt, not a quality grade. Contradiction and ambiguity are welcome when intentional.</p></div><div><div class="_meter_lrrt8_175"><span style="width:0%"></span></div><div class="_metricGrid_lrrt8_190"><div><strong>0<!-- -->/3</strong><span>core compass</span></div><div><strong>0<!-- -->/2</strong><span>image bracket</span></div><div><strong>0<!-- -->/3</strong><span>evidence channels</span></div><div><strong>0<!-- -->/24</strong><span>aligned blocks</span></div></div></div></section><section class="_compassPanel_lrrt8_18"><div class="_sectionHeading_lrrt8_38"><p class="_kicker_lrrt8_62">The contested idea</p><h2>Ask a question the story must earn.</h2><p>Place competing answers under pressure and let choices and consequences create meaning.</p></div><div class="_threeColumns_lrrt8_233"><label class="_field_lrrt8_123"><span>Central question</span><textarea rows="5"></textarea><small>Use a difficult, arguable question—not an automatic moral answer.</small></label><label class="_field_lrrt8_123"><span>Working answer</span><textarea rows="5"></textarea><small>The answer the completed story may support through action and consequence.</small></label><label class="_field_lrrt8_123"><span>Credible counter-answer</span><textarea rows="5"></textarea><small>The opposing belief must be strong enough that intelligent characters could live by it.</small></label></div><div class="_twoColumns_lrrt8_232"><label class="_field_lrrt8_123"><span>Reason to tell this story</span><textarea rows="5"></textarea><small>What should make this story matter to its audience now?</small></label><label class="_field_lrrt8_123"><span>Audience aftertaste</span><textarea rows="5"></textarea><small>Name the feeling or unresolved thought that should remain after the ending.</small></label></div></section><section class="_imageBracket_lrrt8_19"><div class="_sectionHeading_lrrt8_38"><p class="_kicker_lrrt8_62">Opening and closing proof</p><h2>Let the first and last images argue with each other.</h2><p>Their difference should reveal what changed, failed to change, reversed, or remains unresolved.</p></div><div class="_twoColumns_lrrt8_232"><label class="_field_lrrt8_123"><span>Opening image or first impression</span><textarea rows="6"></textarea><small>The starting condition, belief, imbalance, or visual promise.</small></label><label class="_field_lrrt8_123"><span>Closing image or final proof</span><textarea rows="6"></textarea><small>A visible outcome that answers or deliberately complicates the opening.</small></label></div></section><div class="_workspace_lrrt8_273"><section class="_blockPanel_lrrt8_20"><div class="_sectionHeading_lrrt8_38"><p class="_kicker_lrrt8_62">Block <!-- -->1<!-- --> · <!-- -->Hook, Introduction &amp; Catalyst</p><h2>Make this block carry part of the argument.</h2><p>Add the goal, conflict, choice, and consequence in Story Planner so the idea has dramatic pressure.</p></div><div class="_twoColumns_lrrt8_232"><label class="_field_lrrt8_123"><span>Belief under pressure</span><textarea rows="5"></textarea><small>What position changes, hardens, fractures, or becomes visible here?</small></label><label class="_field_lrrt8_123"><span>Audience reframe</span><textarea rows="5"></textarea><small>How does this block change what the audience expects or believes?</small></label><label class="_field_lrrt8_123"><span>Question seed</span><textarea rows="5"></textarea><small>An image, choice, object, relationship, or line that plants meaning for later.</small></label><label class="_field_lrrt8_123"><span>Answer evidence</span><textarea rows="5"></textarea><small>A consequence or callback that gives the seed new meaning without explaining it.</small></label></div><div class="_readOnlyCard_lrrt8_51"><strong>Visible sequence from PageFlow</strong><p>No visual sequence has been recorded for this block yet.</p></div></section><aside class="_characterPanel_lrrt8_21"><div class="_sectionHeading_lrrt8_38"><p class="_kicker_lrrt8_62">Character as argument</p><h2>No character selected</h2><p>Characters test the question by pursuing different wants, protecting different wounds, and paying different prices.</p></div><p class="_empty_lrrt8_330">Add characters in Story Planner to compare their answers to the story question.</p></aside></div><section class="_channelsPanel_lrrt8_22"><div class="_sectionHeading_lrrt8_38"><p class="_kicker_lrrt8_62">Evidence channels</p><h2>Repeat meaning through variation, not repetition.</h2><p>Images, settings, objects and language should approach the same question from different angles.</p></div><div class="_threeColumns_lrrt8_233"><label class="_field_lrrt8_123"><span>Visual and location language</span><textarea rows="8"></textarea><small>Spaces, materials, colours, objects, movement patterns, and environmental contrasts.</small></label><label class="_field_lrrt8_123"><span>Behavioural subtext</span><textarea rows="8"></textarea><small>How characters conceal, redirect, embody, or resist the central question.</small></label><label class="_field_lrrt8_123"><span>Recurring language and motifs</span><textarea rows="8"></textarea><small>Words, images, objects, jokes, rituals, and callbacks whose meaning changes.</small></label></div><div class="_restraintNote_lrrt8_52"><strong>Restraint rule</strong><p>Prefer choices, rewards, losses, reversals and visual callbacks over speeches that explain what the story means. A motif earns its place when its meaning changes.</p></div></section><p class="_status_lrrt8_334" aria-live="polite">Loading the active PlotPickle project…</p></div></main><script id="_R_">import("/assets/index-DBCHrurJ.js")</script></body></html><script>self.__VINEXT_RSC_CHUNKS__=self.__VINEXT_RSC_CHUNKS__||[];self.__VINEXT_RSC_CHUNKS__.push("2:I[\"8c0f216c4604\",[],\"Children\",1]\n3:I[\"f08ec09499bf\",[],\"default\",1]\n4:I[\"96df7669e034\",[],\"default\",1]\n5:I[\"15c18cfaeeff\",[],\"LayoutSegmentProvider\",1]\n6:I[\"8c0f216c4604\",[],\"Slot\",1]\n7:I[\"593f344dc510\",[],\"RedirectBoundary\",1]\n:HL[\"/assets/index-DedKIDsC.css\",\"style\"]\n")</script><script>self.__VINEXT_RSC_CHUNKS__=self.__VINEXT_RSC_CHUNKS__||[];self.__VINEXT_RSC_CHUNKS__.push("0:{\"__route\":\"route:/resonance\",\"__interceptionContext\":null,\"__layoutIds\":[\"layout:/\"],\"__rootLayout\":\"/\",\"page:/resonance\":\"$L1\",\"layout