    </head><body class="__variable_geist_0gdoon9 __variable_geist_mono_08lusff antialiased"><main class="_page_j9tqk_1"><div class="_shell_j9tqk_11"><header class="_header_j9tqk_16"><div><p class="_kicker_j9tqk_61">PlotPickle Playhouse · Whole-draft review workspace</p><h1>DraftLens Engine</h1><p>Read the screenplay as a flexible blueprint, locate what the reader actually experiences, and turn feedback into story-serving questions. Diagnose the root problem before choosing a solution.</p></div><div class="_actions_j9tqk_70"><a href="/" class="_secondaryButton_j9tqk_78">Back to PlotPickle</a><a href="/resonance" class="_secondaryButton_j9tqk_78">Open Resonance</a><a href="/pageflow" class="_secondaryButton_j9tqk_78">Open PageFlow</a><button class="_button_j9tqk_77" type="button">Export project</button></div></header><section class="_projectBar_j9tqk_17"><div class="_projectTitle_j9tqk_110"><strong>Untitled Story</strong><span>Project schema <!-- -->1.7.0<!-- --> · <!-- -->Planning</span></div><label><span>Review block</span><select><option value="1" selected="">Block <!-- -->1<!-- -->: <!-- -->Hook, Introduction &amp; Catalyst</option><option value="2">Block <!-- -->2<!-- -->: <!-- -->Problem, Stakes &amp; Philosophy</option><option value="3">Block <!-- -->3<!-- -->: <!-- -->Anti-theme, Want &amp; Choice</option><option value="4">Block <!-- -->4<!-- -->: <!-- -->Initial Plan, Action &amp; New Problem</option><option value="5">Block <!-- -->5<!-- -->: <!-- -->Adaptation, Revised Plan &amp; Raised Stakes</option><option value="6">Block <!-- -->6<!-- -->: <!-- -->Choice, Action &amp; Antagonist Hint</option><option value="7">Block <!-- -->7<!-- -->: <!-- -->New World &amp; Exploration</option><option value="8">Block <!-- -->8<!-- -->: <!-- -->Action, Rising Tension &amp; Problems</option><option value="9">Block <!-- -->9<!-- -->: <!-- -->Therefore, Choice &amp; Adjusted Plan</option><option value="10">Block <!-- -->10<!-- -->: <!-- -->Raised Stakes, Deeper Question &amp; Action</option><option value="11">Block <!-- -->11<!-- -->: <!-- -->Revelation, Problem &amp; Therefore</option><option value="12">Block <!-- -->12<!-- -->: <!-- -->Midpoint Choice &amp; Action</option><option value="13">Block <!-- -->13<!-- -->: <!-- -->Consequences &amp; Complications</option><option value="14">Block <!-- -->14<!-- -->: <!-- -->Therefore, Choice &amp; Adjusted Plan</option><option value="15">Block <!-- -->15<!-- -->: <!-- -->Major Crisis &amp; All Is Lost</option><option value="16">Block <!-- -->16<!-- -->: <!-- -->Dark Night &amp; Revelation</option><option value="17">Block <!-- -->17<!-- -->: <!-- -->New Choice, Plan &amp; Preparation</option><option value="18">Block <!-- -->18<!-- -->: <!-- -->Action, Climax &amp; Immediate Result</option><option value="19">Block <!-- -->19<!-- -->: <!-- -->Fallout &amp; New Normal</option><option value="20">Block <!-- -->20<!-- -->: <!-- -->Remaining Questions &amp; Actions</option><option value="21">Block <!-- -->21<!-- -->: <!-- -->Final Choice &amp; Last Attempt</option><option value="22">Block <!-- -->22<!-- -->: <!-- -->Final Action &amp; Ultimate Stakes</option><option value="23">Block <!-- -->23<!-- -->: <!-- -->Resolution &amp; New Equilibrium</option><option value="24">Block <!-- -->24<!-- -->: <!-- -->Reflection &amp; Closing Image</option></select></label><label><span>Character lens</span><select disabled=""></select></label></section><section class="_signalPanel_j9tqk_18" aria-label="DraftLens review coverage signal"><div><p class="_kicker_j9tqk_61">Review coverage</p><div class="_signalNumber_j9tqk_166">0<span>/100</span></div><p>This measures preparation and recorded evidence, not whether the screenplay is good or finished.</p></div><div class="_signalDetails_j9tqk_180"><div class="_meter_j9tqk_185"><span style="width:0%"></span></div><div class="_metricGrid_j9tqk_125"><div><strong>0<!-- -->/4</strong><span>story spine</span></div><div><strong>0<!-- -->/4</strong><span>character arcs</span></div><div><strong>0<!-- -->/24</strong><span>causal blocks</span></div><div><strong>0<!-- -->/24</strong><span>drafted blocks</span></div><div><strong>0<!-- -->/4</strong><span>review records</span></div></div></div></section><section class="_summary_po1r4_1" aria-label="Diagnostic craft summary"><div class="_summaryHead_po1r4_8"><div><span>Diagnostic craft</span><strong>4<!-- -->/100</strong></div><a href="/diagnostics">Open full diagnostics</a></div><div class="_summaryCounts_po1r4_5"><div data-severity="problem"><b>23</b><span>root problems</span></div><div data-severity="watch"><b>3</b><span>watch items</span></div><div><b>14</b><span>scene pulse</span></div></div><div class="_compactFindings_po1r4_5"><article class="_finding_po1r4_5" data-severity="problem"><div><span>opening</span><b>problem</b></div><h3>Anchor is not yet doing visible work</h3><p>The audience needs a person, force, value or vulnerability to track.</p><div class="_questions_po1r4_5"><p>Which existing opening action could carry the Anchor effect?</p><p>Would removing the opening damage the story&#x27;s causal, emotional, visual or thematic design?</p></div></article><article class="_finding_po1r4_5" data-severity="problem"><div><span>opening</span><b>problem</b></div><h3>Grip is not yet doing visible work</h3><p>Pressure, contrast or an information gap must make the next moment necessary.</p><div class="_questions_po1r4_5"><p>Which existing opening action could carry the Grip effect?</p><p>Would removing the opening damage the story&#x27;s causal, emotional, visual or thematic design?</p></div></article><article class="_finding_po1r4_5" data-severity="problem"><div><span>opening</span><b>problem</b></div><h3>Compass is not yet doing visible work</h3><p>The opening should let viewers infer a relevant world rule and point of view.</p><div class="_questions_po1r4_5"><p>Which existing opening action could carry the Compass effect?</p><p>Would removing the opening damage the story&#x27;s causal, emotional, visual or thematic design?</p></div></article></div></section><section class="_firstReadPanel_j9tqk_19"><div class="_sectionHeading_j9tqk_40"><p class="_kicker_j9tqk_61">First-read contract</p><h2>Record the experience before trying to repair it.</h2><p>Approach the draft without assuming what it should become. Capture where attention rose, stalled, became confused, or changed direction before proposing revisions.</p></div><label class="_field_j9tqk_121"><span>First-read observations</span><textarea rows="10"></textarea><small>Record the reader experience, strongest impressions, confusion points, emotional turns, and what remains after the read. This uses the shared General Notes field.</small></label></section><section class="_lensesPanel_j9tqk_20"><div class="_sectionHeading_j9tqk_40"><p class="_kicker_j9tqk_61">Six diagnostic lenses</p><h2>Inspect the draft from different angles.</h2><p>A note becomes useful when it identifies the reader experience, the evidence, and the deeper story function involved.</p></div><div class="_lensGrid_j9tqk_257"><article class="_lensCard_j9tqk_122"><span class="_lensNumber_j9tqk_273">01</span><div><h3>Story question</h3><p>Is the central dramatic question established early enough, kept alive, and answered through consequence?</p><small>The dramatic question is not yet defined.</small></div></article><article class="_lensCard_j9tqk_122"><span class="_lensNumber_j9tqk_273">02</span><div><h3>Character engine</h3><p>Does the journey confront the character&#x27;s controlling belief, avoidance pattern, or false solution?</p><small>Add a character in Story Planner to inspect the character engine.</small></div></article><article class="_lensCard_j9tqk_122"><span class="_lensNumber_j9tqk_273">03</span><div><h3>Structure and pattern</h3><p>Do cause, choice, escalation, repetition and surprise create forward movement rather than mechanical plot points?</p><small>Add goal, conflict, choice or action, and consequence to this block.</small></div></article><article class="_lensCard_j9tqk_122"><span class="_lensNumber_j9tqk_273">04</span><div><h3>Page experience</h3><p>Is the action clear and compelling? Does each page create a reason to continue rather than merely transmit information?</p><small>No page draft has been recorded for this block.</small></div></article><article class="_lensCard_j9tqk_122"><span class="_lensNumber_j9tqk_273">05</span><div><h3>Dialogue and exposition</h3><p>Do characters speak from distinct viewpoints while information enters through desire, pressure, status, humour, or action?</p><small>No dialogue rule has been recorded yet.</small></div></article><article class="_lensCard_j9tqk_122"><span class="_lensNumber_j9tqk_273">06</span><div><h3>Surprise and specificity</h3><p>Does the story travel an earned but unexpected route, or is it repeating familiar territory without a distinctive turn?</p><small>No audience reframe has been recorded.</small></div></article></div></section><div class="_workspace_j9tqk_301"><section class="_blockPanel_j9tqk_21"><div class="_sectionHeading_j9tqk_40"><p class="_kicker_j9tqk_61">Block <!-- -->1<!-- --> · <!-- -->Hook, Introduction &amp; Catalyst</p><h2>Separate the visible symptom from the root cause.</h2><p>Complete the block cause-and-effect spine before diagnosing the scene.</p></div><label class="_field_j9tqk_121"><span>Block review note</span><textarea rows="13"></textarea><small>Describe the reader experience and cite the story evidence. Ask what may be causing it before prescribing a rewrite. This edits the block&#x27;s shared notes.</small></label><div class="_evidenceCards_j9tqk_124"><article><span>PageFlow draft</span><p>No page text recorded.</p></article><article><span>Visible sequence</span><p>No visual sequence recorded.</p></article><article><span>Audience turn</span><p>No audience turn recorded.</p></article></div></section><aside class="_characterPanel_j9tqk_22"><div class="_sectionHeading_j9tqk_40"><p class="_kicker_j9tqk_61">Selected character</p><h2>No character selected</h2><p>The plot should challenge the character&#x27;s current strategy, not merely move them between events.</p></div><p class="_empty_j9tqk_374">Add characters in Story Planner to inspect the character journey.</p></aside></div><section class="_rootNotePanel_j9tqk_23"><div class="_sectionHeading_j9tqk_40"><p class="_kicker_j9tqk_61">The note beneath the note</p><h2>Diagnose broadly; revise specifically.</h2><p>A weak moment may be a symptom of an earlier setup, unclear objective, missing consequence, inconsistent worldview, or delayed story question. Preserve multiple possible solutions until the root problem is understood.</p></div><div class="_twoColumns_j9tqk_345"><label class="_field_j9tqk_121"><span>Root diagnosis and revision priorities</span><textarea rows="11"></textarea><small>Name what appears to be structurally wrong, why it matters, and what must improve. Avoid locking the writer into one proposed fix.</small></label><label class="_field_j9tqk_121"><span>Questions for the next draft</span><textarea rows="11"></textarea><small>Use precise questions that expose uncertainty: What does the character want here? What changes? Why now? What evidence earns the turn?</small></label><label class="_field_j9tqk_121"><span>Continuity and evidence log</span><textarea rows="9"></textarea><small>Record page, block, character, object, location, setup, payoff, or behaviour evidence supporting the diagnosis.</small></label><label class="_field_j9tqk_121"><span>Comparisons and research</span><textarea rows="9"></textarea><small>Record useful craft references or comparable patterns without turning them into instructions to imitate another story.</small></label><label class="_field_j9tqk_121"><span>Feedback sources</span><textarea rows="8"></textarea><small>Identify readers, dates, drafts, table reads, observations, or testing conditions so repeated notes can be compared in context.</small></label></div></section><section class="_protocolPanel_j9tqk_24"><div class="_sectionHeading_j9tqk_40"><p class="_kicker_j9tqk_61">Notes protocol</p><h2>Serve the story without taking ownership away from the writer.</h2></div><ol><li><strong>Observe first.</strong><span>Describe the experience before interpreting it.</span></li><li><strong>Be script-specific.</strong><span>Generic advice is weaker than evidence tied to these characters and this story.</span></li><li><strong>Trace the root.</strong><span>A confusing moment may begin several blocks earlier.</span></li><li><strong>Diagnose before prescribing.</strong><span>State what is not working and why; preserve more than one solution.</span></li><li><strong>Ask useful questions.</strong><span>A precise question can unlock a stronger answer than a replacement scene.</span></li><li><strong>Cool down.</strong><span>When receiving difficult feedback, separate the emotional reaction from the possible truth inside the note.</span></li></ol></section><p class="_status_j9tqk_381" aria-live="polite">Loading the active PlotPickle project…</p></div></main><script id="_R_">import("/assets/index-DBCHrurJ.js")</script></body></html><script>self.__VINEXT_RSC_CHUNKS__=self.__VINEXT_RSC_CHUNKS__||[];self.__VINEXT_RSC_CHUNKS__.push("2:I[\"8c0f216c4604\",[],\"Children\",1]\n3:I[\"f08ec09499bf\",[],\"default\",1]\n4:I[\"96df7669e034\",[],\"default\",1]\n5:I[\"15c18cfaeeff\",[],\"LayoutSegmentProvider\",1]\n6:I[\"8c0f216c4604\",[],\"Slot\",1]\n7:I[\"593f344dc510\",[],\"RedirectBoundary\",1]\n:HL[\"/assets/index-DedKIDsC.css\",\"style\"]\n")</script><script>self.__VINEXT_RSC_CHUNKS__=self.__VINEXT_RSC_CHUNKS__||[];self.__VINEXT_RSC_CHUNKS__.push("0:{\"__route\":\"route:/draftlens\",\"__interceptionContext\":null,\"__layoutIds\":[\"layout:/\"],\"__rootLayout\":\"/\",\"page:/draftlens\":\"$L1\",\"layout:/\":[[[[\"$\",\"link\",\"css:/assets/index-DedKIDsC.css\",{\"rel\":\"stylesheet\",\"precedence\":\"vite-rsc/importer-resources\",\"href\":\"/assets/index-DedKIDsC.css\",\"dat