    </head><body class="__variable_geist_0gdoon9 __variable_geist_mono_08lusff antialiased"><main class="_page_15jet_1"><div class="_shell_15jet_10"><header class="_header_15jet_17"><div><p class="_kicker_15jet_70">PlotPickle Playhouse · Deliberate-practice workspace</p><h1>CraftLoop Engine</h1><p>Apply the complete method to one block: engage the audience, establish the contract, turn the scene, increase character-specific pressure, observe human language, compress the page, and explain the story clearly.</p></div><div class="_actions_15jet_79"><a href="/" class="_secondaryButton_15jet_89">Back to PlotPickle</a><a href="/resonance" class="_secondaryButton_15jet_89">Resonance</a><a href="/voiceprint" class="_secondaryButton_15jet_89">Voiceprint</a><a href="/pageflow" class="_secondaryButton_15jet_89">PageFlow</a><a href="/draftlens" class="_secondaryButton_15jet_89">DraftLens</a><button class="_button_15jet_88" type="button">Export project</button></div></header><section class="_projectBar_15jet_18"><div class="_projectTitle_15jet_125"><strong>Untitled Story</strong><span>Project schema <!-- -->1.7.0<!-- --> · <!-- -->Planning</span></div><label><span>Practice block</span><select><option value="1" selected="">Block <!-- -->1<!-- -->: <!-- -->Hook, Introduction &amp; Catalyst</option><option value="2">Block <!-- -->2<!-- -->: <!-- -->Problem, Stakes &amp; Philosophy</option><option value="3">Block <!-- -->3<!-- -->: <!-- -->Anti-theme, Want &amp; Choice</option><option value="4">Block <!-- -->4<!-- -->: <!-- -->Initial Plan, Action &amp; New Problem</option><option value="5">Block <!-- -->5<!-- -->: <!-- -->Adaptation, Revised Plan &amp; Raised Stakes</option><option value="6">Block <!-- -->6<!-- -->: <!-- -->Choice, Action &amp; Antagonist Hint</option><option value="7">Block <!-- -->7<!-- -->: <!-- -->New World &amp; Exploration</option><option value="8">Block <!-- -->8<!-- -->: <!-- -->Action, Rising Tension &amp; Problems</option><option value="9">Block <!-- -->9<!-- -->: <!-- -->Therefore, Choice &amp; Adjusted Plan</option><option value="10">Block <!-- -->10<!-- -->: <!-- -->Raised Stakes, Deeper Question &amp; Action</option><option value="11">Block <!-- -->11<!-- -->: <!-- -->Revelation, Problem &amp; Therefore</option><option value="12">Block <!-- -->12<!-- -->: <!-- -->Midpoint Choice &amp; Action</option><option value="13">Block <!-- -->13<!-- -->: <!-- -->Consequences &amp; Complications</option><option value="14">Block <!-- -->14<!-- -->: <!-- -->Therefore, Choice &amp; Adjusted Plan</option><option value="15">Block <!-- -->15<!-- -->: <!-- -->Major Crisis &amp; All Is Lost</option><option value="16">Block <!-- -->16<!-- -->: <!-- -->Dark Night &amp; Revelation</option><option value="17">Block <!-- -->17<!-- -->: <!-- -->New Choice, Plan &amp; Preparation</option><option value="18">Block <!-- -->18<!-- -->: <!-- -->Action, Climax &amp; Immediate Result</option><option value="19">Block <!-- -->19<!-- -->: <!-- -->Fallout &amp; New Normal</option><option value="20">Block <!-- -->20<!-- -->: <!-- -->Remaining Questions &amp; Actions</option><option value="21">Block <!-- -->21<!-- -->: <!-- -->Final Choice &amp; Last Attempt</option><option value="22">Block <!-- -->22<!-- -->: <!-- -->Final Action &amp; Ultimate Stakes</option><option value="23">Block <!-- -->23<!-- -->: <!-- -->Resolution &amp; New Equilibrium</option><option value="24">Block <!-- -->24<!-- -->: <!-- -->Reflection &amp; Closing Image</option></select></label><label><span>Character pressure</span><select disabled=""></select></label></section><section class="_signalPanel_15jet_19" aria-label="CraftLoop practice coverage signal"><div><p class="_kicker_15jet_70">Practice coverage</p><div class="_signalNumber_15jet_178">0<span>/100</span></div><p>This measures whether enough evidence exists for a complete practice pass. It is not a quality grade.</p></div><div class="_signalDetails_15jet_194"><div class="_meter_15jet_200"><span style="width:0%"></span></div><div class="_metricGrid_15jet_214"><div><strong>0<!-- -->/7</strong><span>audience game</span></div><div><strong>0<!-- -->/6</strong><span>opening contract</span></div><div><strong>0<!-- -->/5</strong><span>scene turn</span></div><div><strong>0<!-- -->/5</strong><span>character pressure</span></div><div><strong>0<!-- -->/4</strong><span>human voice</span></div><div><strong>0<!-- -->/4</strong><span>page evidence</span></div><div><strong>0<!-- -->/2</strong><span>pitch clarity</span></div></div></div></section><section class="_panel_15jet_20"><div class="_sectionHeading_15jet_39"><p class="_kicker_15jet_70">Pass 1 · Audience game</p><h2>Give the audience something active to track.</h2><p>Define the live question, the expected route, and the block-level change in audience belief.</p></div><div class="_twoColumns_15jet_259"><label class="_field_15jet_141"><span>Central tension</span><textarea rows="6"></textarea><small>What unresolved force keeps the story active?</small></label><label class="_field_15jet_141"><span>Audience question</span><textarea rows="6"></textarea><small>What is the audience trying to solve, predict, or understand?</small></label><label class="_field_15jet_141"><span>Expected destination</span><textarea rows="6"></textarea><small>Where does the audience currently think the story is going?</small></label><label class="_field_15jet_141"><span>Unpredictable route</span><textarea rows="6"></textarea><small>How can the journey remain earned without becoming obvious?</small></label><label class="_field_15jet_141"><span>Block 1 audience expectation</span><textarea rows="6"></textarea><small>What does the audience believe before this block turns?</small></label><label class="_field_15jet_141"><span>Block 1 reframe</span><textarea rows="6"></textarea><small>What clue, reversal, complication, or near-answer changes that belief?</small></label></div></section><section class="_panel_15jet_20"><div class="_sectionHeading_15jet_39"><p class="_kicker_15jet_70">Pass 2 · Opening contract</p><h2>Introduce enough to create trust and curiosity.</h2><p>The opening should establish image, world, character pressure, question, and promise without explaining everything.</p></div><div class="_twoColumns_15jet_259"><label class="_field_15jet_141"><span>Opening hook</span><textarea rows="6"></textarea><small>The first compelling image, condition, action, or contradiction.</small></label><label class="_field_15jet_141"><span>Ordinary world</span><textarea rows="6"></textarea><small>The normal pattern the story is about to disturb.</small></label><label class="_field_15jet_141"><span>Catalyst</span><textarea rows="6"></textarea><small>The disruption that changes what the protagonist can continue doing.</small></label><label class="_field_15jet_141"><span>Theme pressure</span><textarea rows="6"></textarea><small>The question or competing belief the opening begins to test.</small></label></div><div class="_evidenceGrid_15jet_283"><article class="_evidenceCard_15jet_53"><span>Block 1 purpose</span><p>Open with a compelling image, establish the protagonist&#x27;s ordinary world, then disrupt it.</p></article><article class="_evidenceCard_15jet_53"><span>Block 1 summary</span><p>No opening summary recorded.</p></article><article class="_evidenceCard_15jet_53"><span>Block 1 conflict</span><p>No opening conflict recorded.</p></article><article class="_evidenceCard_15jet_53"><span>Opening image progression</span><p>No opening visual sequence recorded.</p></article></div></section><div class="_workspace_15jet_310"><section class="_panel_15jet_20"><div class="_sectionHeading_15jet_39"><p class="_kicker_15jet_70">Pass 3 · Scene turn</p><h2>Make Block <!-- -->1<!-- --> end differently than it began.</h2><p>Information matters most when it changes intention, power, understanding, risk, or action.</p></div><label class="_field_15jet_141"><span>Goal or immediate condition</span><textarea rows="6"></textarea><small>What is the character trying to accomplish or preserve?</small></label><label class="_field_15jet_141"><span>Conflict and resistance</span><textarea rows="6"></textarea><small>What specifically stands in the way?</small></label><div class="_twoColumns_15jet_259"><label class="_field_15jet_141"><span>Choice</span><textarea rows="6"></textarea><small>What decision reveals strategy or character?</small></label><label class="_field_15jet_141"><span>Action</span><textarea rows="6"></textarea><small>What does the character actually do?</small></label><label class="_field_15jet_141"><span>Consequence</span><textarea rows="6"></textarea><small>What becomes newly true because of that action or choice?</small></label><label class="_field_15jet_141"><span>Emotional turn</span><textarea rows="6"></textarea><small>How does the felt meaning or relationship change?</small></label></div></section><aside class="_characterPanel_15jet_23"><div class="_sectionHeading_15jet_39"><p class="_kicker_15jet_70">Pass 4 · Character pressure</p><h2>No character selected</h2><p>Increase difficulty by attacking this character&#x27;s strategy, belief, status, relationship, or emotional limit.</p></div><p class="_empty_15jet_323">Add a character in Story Planner to run the pressure pass.</p></aside></div><section class="_panel_15jet_20"><div class="_sectionHeading_15jet_39"><p class="_kicker_15jet_70">Pass 5 · Human voice</p><h2>Observe motive, rhythm, silence, and status.</h2><p>Look beyond the obvious reason for a line. People often speak from several motives at the same time.</p></div><div class="_twoColumns_15jet_259"><label class="_field_15jet_141"><span>Selected character voice</span><textarea rows="8"></textarea><small>The concise scene-ready voice rule shared with Voiceprint.</small></label><label class="_field_15jet_141"><span>Fieldwork observations</span><textarea rows="8"></textarea><small>Record cadence, fillers, corrections, silence, topic changes, and status shifts observed in real speech.</small></label><label class="_field_15jet_141"><span>Subtext strategy</span><textarea rows="8"></textarea><small>What is concealed, redirected, negotiated, or communicated indirectly?</small></label><article class="_evidenceCard_15jet_53"><span>Voice contrast</span><p>No project-wide voice contrast recorded.</p></article></div></section><section class="_pagePanel_15jet_21"><div class="_sectionHeading_15jet_39"><p class="_kicker_15jet_70">Pass 6 · Page compression</p><h2>Make every word create visible movement.</h2><p>Use active verbs, concrete evidence, useful white space, and precise image progression.</p></div><div class="_pageWorkspace_15jet_334"><label class="_field_15jet_141"><span>Page draft</span><textarea rows="18"></textarea><small>Shared PageFlow screenplay text for this block.</small></label><aside class="_pageSignal_15jet_55"><div class="_pageScore_15jet_187">100<span>/100</span></div><p>PageFlow editorial signal</p><div class="_stats_15jet_358"><span>0<!-- --> words</span><span>0<!-- --> action paragraphs</span><span>0<!-- --> words per sentence</span></div><p class="_empty_15jet_323">No current PageFlow signals. Continue refining for voice and dramatic effect.</p></aside></div><label class="_field_15jet_141"><span>Visible sequence</span><textarea rows="8"></textarea><small>The image progression shared with PageFlow and Visual Board.</small></label></section><section class="_panel_15jet_20"><div class="_sectionHeading_15jet_39"><p class="_kicker_15jet_70">Pass 7 · Pitch and reflect</p><h2>Explain the story with confidence and remain open to discovery.</h2><p>A pitch tests whether the story engine is clear. Craft study should produce an original experiment, not imitation.</p></div><div class="_twoColumns_15jet_259"><label class="_field_15jet_141"><span>One-sentence pitch</span><textarea rows="5"></textarea><small>The clearest statement of protagonist, pressure, action, stakes, and distinction.</small></label><label class="_field_15jet_141"><span>Short spoken pitch</span><textarea rows="9"></textarea><small>A concise, energetic explanation that communicates the experience without pretending every solution is fixed.</small></label><label class="_field_15jet_141"><span>Comparative craft study</span><textarea rows="10"></textarea><small>Record a technique observed in produced work, the principle underneath it, and how you will test that principle originally. This shares the project Research field.</small></label><article class="_evidenceCard_15jet_53"><span>Signature execution</span><p>Define the distinctive move that makes this project recognizably itself.</p></article></div></section><section class="_loopPanel_15jet_22"><div class="_sectionHeading_15jet_39"><p class="_kicker_15jet_70">Repeatable studio loop</p><h2>Practise with evidence, not just advice.</h2></div><ol><li><strong>Audience.</strong><span>What are viewers tracking and what changes their belief?</span></li><li><strong>Opening.</strong><span>What promise, image, world, character, and pressure are established?</span></li><li><strong>Turn.</strong><span>What becomes different because this block happened?</span></li><li><strong>Pressure.</strong><span>Why is this obstacle uniquely difficult for this character?</span></li><li><strong>Voice.</strong><span>What motive, rhythm, silence, and status are audible?</span></li><li><strong>Page.</strong><span>Can the action become more visible, active, precise, and economical?</span></li><li><strong>Pitch.</strong><span>Can the writer communicate the story clearly and still remain flexible?</span></li></ol></section><p class="_status_15jet_429" aria-live="polite">Loading the active PlotPickle project…</p></div></main><script id="_R_">import("/assets/index-DBCHrurJ.js")</script></body></html><script>self.__VINEXT_RSC_CHUNKS__=self.__VINEXT_RSC_CHUNKS__||[];self.__VINEXT_RSC_CHUNKS__.push("2:I[\"8c0f216c4604\",[],\"Children\",1]\n3:I[\"f08ec09499bf\",[],\"default\",1]\n4:I[\"96df7669e034\",[],\"default\",1]\n5:I[\"15c18cfaeeff\",[],\"LayoutSegmentPr